        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">cPanel/WHM ($15-45/month)</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">The one everyone knows. If you have ever used shared hosting, this is
          probably what you used. Works great, but they keep jacking up the price and it hurts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">Plesk ($10-45/month)</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">More modern than cPanel, comes with WordPress tools built in, and actually
          works on Windows servers if you swing that way. Increasingly my recommendation over cPanel.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">CyberPanel (Free)</h4>
        <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-2">Cannot beat free. It is open source, runs on LiteSpeed, and does the job.
          Not as pretty as the paid options but your wallet will thank you.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/5 border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
        <h4 class="text-white font-semibold">RunCloud ($8-15/month)</h4>
